{"skill":{"slug":"todoist","displayName":"Todoist"},"version":{"version":"0.2.1","createdAt":1769577779661,"changelog":"Tweak ordering instructions","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3110,"sha256":"56960995964fa8cf3110194b53dfbba90283a402585f89325414d2dfa72eb731","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1959,"sha256":"5f86cc02337b040475fa5e201718454d3a7c5456042a3cf8414292a39cb5e306","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015102597,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3b69e575f11a7c79036e76ddb7b1da5caf1e0d41b06cf0fd5e5858d8f6578b05","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3b69e575f11a7c79036e76ddb7b1da5caf1e0d41b06cf0fd5e5858d8f6578b05","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: todoist\nVersion: 0.2.1\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It provides instructions for installing and using the `todoist-ts-cli` to manage Todoist tasks. All commands and usage examples are directly related to Todoist functionality. The `SKILL.md` file requires an external npm package (`todoist-ts-cli`) for installation, which is a standard dependency management practice and does not inherently indicate malicious intent within this skill bundle. It also correctly specifies the need for a `TODOIST_API_TOKEN` environment variable for authentication, which is a secure practice. There are no signs of data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts against the agent, or other malicious behaviors.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159670936},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":18,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789015102597},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This Todoist skill is mostly coherent, but it asks users to install an unpinned global CLI and handle a Todoist API token in ways that deserve review before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Requiring a Todoist API token is proportionate for Todoist account access, but the documented token setup includes command-line and environment-variable handling that can expose the credential through shell history, process metadata, or environment capture.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The installation command uses a global npm install with a semver range, so the installed third-party CLI package may differ from what was reviewed and will be available system-wide for the installing user.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The activation text covers broad task, reminder, and productivity requests, which may route generic task-management requests to Todoist even when the user did not explicitly name Todoist.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill documents persistent authentication and destructive Todoist actions such as delete without explicit confirmation or identity-verification guidance, creating avoidable risk of accidental account-data changes.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill's capabilities fit its stated Todoist task-management purpose, including listing, adding, updating, completing, moving, commenting on, and deleting tasks.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable granting CLI access to your Todoist account. Prefer a pinned, reviewed CLI version, avoid running npm install with elevated privileges, avoid placing your API token directly in shell history, and verify task IDs before completing, moving, or deleting tasks.","findings":"[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad activation wording is not malicious, but it is wider than necessary for a third-party account integration and could cause unintended Todoist access for generic productivity requests.\n[SQP-2] expected: Task mutation commands are expected for a Todoist management skill, but the artifact does not tell the agent to confirm ambiguous matches or destructive deletes before acting.\n[T08] unexpected: A CLI dependency is expected, but the unpinned global npm installation is broader and less reproducible than needed for a reviewed skill.\n[T09] expected: A Todoist token is expected for the integration, but entering it directly as a command argument or exporting it in the shell is a credential-handling weakness.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015102597}}}}}